=begin rakudoc :!toc
=TITLE RakuDoc Editor
=for AUTHOR :hidden
Richard N. Hainsworth, aka finanalyst
=for LICENSE :hidden
Artistic-2.0
=VERSION v0.1.0

=head Overview

This repo contains the files needed to create a Docker image that when run
locally will allow a browser to create an edit a RakuDoc source file.

A directory is needed into which the source file is copied, eg. C<~/rakudoc-test>.

The container is deployed by running the following inside the directory.

    podman run -v .:browser/publication docker.io/finanalyst/browser-editor:latest

The sample file C<sample.rakudoc> is copied into the directory. Inside the browser, the sample
file can be edited or a new one created, and the file name can be changed.

The I<web-browser-editor> files are intended for use on a server publicly accessible.
The container created by C<Web.dockerfile> is intended to be placed behind an Apache or nginx
reverse-proxy.

The following is a sample extract from an Apache2 conf file:
=begin code
    ProxyRequests Off
    ProxyVia on

    RewriteEngine on
    RewriteCond %{HTTP:Connection} Upgrade [NC]

    RewriteRule (/'browser-socket'.*) ws://127.0.0.1:12345/$1 [P,L]

    RewriteEngine off

    ProxyPass /browser-socket ws://127.0.0.1:12345/browser-socket
    ProxyPassReverse /browser-socket ws://127.0.0.1:12345/browser-socket
    ProxyPass /rakudoc_editor/ http://127.0.0.1:12345/

    ProxyPass /browser-socket ws://127.0.0.1:12345/browser-socket
    ProxyPassReverse /browser-socket ws://127.0.0.1:12345/browser-socket
    ProxyPass /rakudoc_editor/ http://127.0.0.1:12345/
    ProxyPassReverse /rakudoc_editor/ http://127.0.0.1:12345/
=end code

The browser is given a URL C<www.example.com/rakudoc_editor/> the final C</> is important.
Finally, the container is started as follows:
=begin code
sudo docker pull docker.io/finanalyst/rakudoc_browser:latest
sudo docker run -d -p 12345:3000 --rm docker.io/finanalyst/rakudoc_browser
=end code

The C<3000> is the port being listened to by the Cro server defined by C<WebServeBrowser.raku>

